  "report_period": "Week 22 (22nd May to 29th May 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Nissen Kaiun have committed the Capesize \"Ehime Queen\" 181/2016 Imabari, Japan (SS 07/2031, DD 05/2029, Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 57,5 mill basis delivery July-September 2026. Note that the three-years-younger sister vessel \"Lowlands Spirit\" 182/2019 Imabari, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 65,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Panagia Force\" 81/2007 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 04/2027) of Polforce Shipping was committed at USD 13,5 mill. Remind you that back in March, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"ASL Moon\" 81/2008 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) was sold at USD 13,6 mill. On the Panamax sector, the \"Exelixsea\" 76/2011 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 09/2026) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 17,5 mill. For reference, the \"Global Bonanza\" 75/2011 Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026) was sold back in January at USD 15,3 mill. Zhejiang Shipping group have committed their Ultramax \"Tian Mu Shan\" & \"Yan Dang Shan\" 63/2017 Sainty, China (SS/DD 01/2027 & SS/DD 06/2027) via online bidding at USD 52,32 mill enbloc, while the \"Beltiger\" 63/2017 New Times, China (SS/DD 01/2027) from Belships was committed at USD 26,8 mill. The Supramax \"Ausone\" 56/2012 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 04/2027) was committed at USD 14 mill and the \"Sea Affluence\" 56/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS 04/2030, DD 06/2028) was committed at xs USD 15 mill. In addition, the \"Jade\" 55/2010 NACKS, China (SS 04/2030, DD 04/2028) was committed to Turkish interests at low USD 15 mill. Note that the sister vessel \"Coral Gem\" 55/2010 NACKS, China (SS 02/2030, DD 07/2027) was sold back in March at USD 14,5 mill. Mariners Shipping Agency have committed the Handysize \"Despina K\" 32/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 05/2030, DD 09/2028) to undisclosed interests at USD 9,2 mill. Remind you that back in March, the \"Sea Sapphire\" 32/2010 Zhejiang, China (SS 03/2030, DD 05/2028) was sold at USD 8,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "OKEE Maritime have committed their MR2 \"Okee John T\" 53/2006 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 02/2031, DD 03/2029) at xs USD 16 mill. Remind you that same owners sold the sister vessel \"Okee Ulf\" 53/2006 Shin Kurushima, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) back in January at USD 12,9 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the Singapore-Japan range were reported between usd 20,000/23,000 pd. A number of Australian trips from South China into Singapore-Japan range were fixed at levels ranging from usd 23,000/25,000 pd. South East Asian trips to China and Singapore-Japan were noticed between usd 20,000/24,000 pd. East Coast South American trips to Singapore-Japan and Far East range were reported at usd 22,000/24,000 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed between usd 20,000/21,000 pd for 5/7 months.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "South East Asia trips into East Coast India were reported at a range of usd 18,000/19,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into Singapore were fixed at usd 17,000/18,000 pd. East Coast South American trips via Persian Gulf and East Coast South America into Continent-Mediterranean were fixed at usd 28,000/30,000 pd. US Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at usd 20,000 pd. US East Coast trips into Mediterranean and South East Asia we reported at usd 25,000/28,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Australian trips into China were reported at usd 16,000 pd, while North China trips into South East Asia and East Coast India were fixed at a range of usd 19,000/20,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were reported at usd 12,000/14,000 pd. West Coast Central American trips into Singapore- Japan range were fixed at usd 17,000/19,000 pd."
    }
  },
